            <ArticleTitle>Benign acute childhood myositis: an unusual cause of calf pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>703-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00247-008-0785-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a 17-year-old boy with benign acute childhood myositis (BACM) who presented with acute onset of right calf pain, swelling, and difficulty walking. The MR findings are reviewed. MR may be useful in diagnosing BACM and in differentiating it from other causes of myositis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
